{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["\"וַיַּרְא אֱלֹהִים אֶת הָאוֹר\" — He examined its appearance, that it was fine. And likewise: וַתֵּרֶא אֹתוֹ כִּי טוֹב הוּא — she examined Moshe, who was born after six months, like Shmuel at the turn of the year, and she saw that he was fine and beautiful, because his features and his nails and his hair were fully formed. And she hid him three months — that is, until the end of nine months, for she had examined him and knew that he was fine and beautiful in his features, that he was not a miscarriage." "\"וַיַּבְדֵּל אֱלֹהִים בֵּין הָאוֹר וּבֵין הַחֹשֶׁךְ\" — The day was twelve hours, and afterward the night twelve. The light first, and afterward the darkness. For the beginning of the world's creation was with the utterance ״יְהִי אוֹר״. And all the darkness that preceded this — as it is written: ״וְחֹשֶׁךְ עַל פְּנֵי תְהוֹם״ — is not what is called night."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:16:32.179599572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}